<title>GERMANY: German parlt starts debate on austerity package.</title>
<headline>German parlt starts debate on austerity package.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German lower house of parliament on Friday began its final debate on some key parts of the government's austerity programme which was expected to last only a few hours.</p>
<p>Votes on health and pension system reforms as well as plans to cut sick pay and reduce workers' protection from firing were expected by 1300 GMT at the latest.</p>
<p>The cuts being voted on would account for nearly a third of Bonn's planned 70 billion marks of public spending cuts for next year.</p>
<p>-- Ashley Seager, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
